+      assertion, which reds instead of printing a green line over nothing.
+      That case is the gate's own subject, so it is pinned by a test fixture
+      too (`a table that parses to zero rows reds rather than exiting green`).
+      No `canary:` recipe: this gate's only violation shape is a MODIFICATION of
+      a tracked artefact (`docs/MIGRATION.md`), and the canary contract is
+      create-only, so it reports UNPROVEN rather than green. Discrimination is
+      proven instead by paired fixtures in
+      `tests/scripts/lint_scheduled_deprecations.test.ts`, verified by mutation:
+      widening the overdue threshold fails the overdue-by-construction case, and
+      granting `allowEmpty` fails the zero-row case.
